  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "The six faces of a die are numbered $-3,-2,-1,0,1,2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If the die is rolled twice and the two numbers are multiplied together, then what is the probability that the result is negative?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
          "worked": "There are three negative faces and two positive faces. A negative product requires one of each, in either order; any zero gives a zero product.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of favourable outcomes}&=3\\times2+2\\times3\\\\\\text{Number of favourable outcomes}&=12\\\\\\Pr(\\text{negative product})&=\\frac{12}{6^2}=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q20-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What if the die is rolled three times?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{24}$\n\nCount outcomes with one negative and two positives, or three negatives.",
          "worked": "A negative product requires one negative and two positives, or three negatives. Zero cannot occur. The single negative can occupy any of the three positions.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of favourable outcomes}&=3\\times(3\\times2\\times2)+3\\times3\\times3\\\\\\text{Number of favourable outcomes}&=36+27=63\\\\\\Pr(\\text{negative product})&=\\frac{63}{6^3}=\\frac{7}{24}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
